window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"urgot","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Urgot","Urgot","Skill","Urgot","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Full Corrosive Charge plus Purge gives you shred DPS and a zoning slow that wins every trade - this is your window to break the lane open and deny his farm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fear Beyond Death threatens every low trade he takes, but his R Final Retribution flips a fight he starts first - play threshold chicken and never dip below half without your E up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your bruiser item keeps you the stronger sustained fighter; keep the W uptime pressure on before his two-item burst rotation matures."},{"when":"2 items","text":"His reset Q poke and empowered E now out-rotate your clunky combo and his R heals through your DPS - stop dueling, hold E Disdain for his engage, and call for help."}],"wants":{"you":["W Purge uptime controlling every wave","E Disdain flip answering his E Golden Onslaught","Fights ended at your R threshold, not his"],"foe":["Q Darkin Glaive poke from outside Purge range","A two-item game where his rotation outpaces yours","R Final Retribution cast before your chains land"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are quiet - your shotgun legs make his careless autos costly but neither kit is assembled, so trade lightly and stack the wave. From 3 you take command: Corrosive Charge into Purge shreds him inside your zone and the slow means he cannot leave a trade he is losing, so bleed him every rotation.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay yours as W uptime and the Q-E flip control both the lane and his income. Level 6 turns into threshold chicken: your Fear Beyond Death executes any trade that dips him low, but his R Final Retribution wins any fight he starts on his terms - track his cooldowns and only commit with E Disdain in your pocket.","late":"Your first item keeps you the stronger sustained bruiser and that is the era to force fights, because two items in the lane flips: his Q resets and empowered E Golden Onslaught out-rotate your combo while R Final Retribution heals him through your Purge - late, you peel with the flip and let your team answer him.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm, though your shotgun-leg passive makes his careless autos costly.","Level 2 stays neutral - your Purge shred and his burst combo are both incomplete.","Level 3 is yours: full Corrosive Charge and Purge give you shred DPS and a zoning slow that win trades.","Levels 4-5 stay yours as W uptime and the Q-E flip control the lane and his farm.","Level 6 is even - your Fear Beyond Death execute threatens every low trade, so it hinges on threshold play.","On your first item your shred and flip-combo pressure keep you the stronger sustained bruiser.","Two items in he takes over - Q resets and empowered E outpace your rotation while his R heals through your DPS."]});
